  "abstract": "This experiment is the first step in a new research program exploring a \"Modular Graph\" paradigm. It tests the core hypothesis that a learned, differentiable clustering of neurons is a valid and effective inductive bias. This model uses a trainable matrix to pool 71k neurons into 256 clusters, forecasts the cluster dynamics with a simple shared MLP, and unpools the results. It deliberately omits any graph-based message passing to isolate the effect of the clustering mechanism itself.",
  "submitted_tick": 87,
  "no_debugger": false,
  "cpu_only": false,
